1
00:00:12,887 --> 00:00:15,724
AS YOU STOOD BY

2
00:00:17,434 --> 00:00:20,270
EUN-SU, HUI-SU AND JIN SO-BAEK

3
00:00:40,415 --> 00:00:42,125
Pop open the trunk for a second.

4
00:00:52,093 --> 00:00:54,345
Let's do this before the ambulances come.

5
00:00:57,057 --> 00:00:59,309
I need you to open the trunk, ma'am.

6
00:01:04,481 --> 00:01:05,690
Open up.

7
00:01:09,694 --> 00:01:11,945
- Kim, over here!
- Uh, coming, sir.

8
00:01:15,825 --> 00:01:17,534
Let's clear a path. Hurry!

9
00:01:32,133 --> 00:01:34,135
Sure you don't need me
to come up with you?

10
00:01:34,636 --> 00:01:35,887
Mm-hmm.

11
00:01:37,472 --> 00:01:38,473
Okay.

12
00:01:39,182 --> 00:01:42,227
Just make yourself some soup,
then try to get some rest.

13
00:01:43,144 --> 00:01:44,229
You too.

14
00:01:45,355 --> 00:01:47,023
Hui-su...

15
00:01:52,946 --> 00:01:53,988
You're okay.

16
00:02:28,565 --> 00:02:34,571
MR. NOH JIN-PYO

17
00:02:49,836 --> 00:02:53,965
RECIPIENT: MR. NOH JIN-PYO

18
00:03:12,734 --> 00:03:16,028
- <i>Hey, nice shot.</i>
- <i>She's really improved her game.</i>

19
00:03:16,029 --> 00:03:17,362
<i>The polar bear...</i>

20
00:03:17,363 --> 00:03:18,739
<i>A good stance is important,</i>

21
00:03:18,740 --> 00:03:21,700
<i>as it provides a solid base
for generating power. Feet should be...</i>

22
00:03:21,701 --> 00:03:24,161
<i>...lowest readings you've seen.
Typically, you find...</i>

23
00:03:32,253 --> 00:03:34,004
<i>The questions
we need to ask ourselves</i>

24
00:03:34,005 --> 00:03:35,797
<i>are why are you letting him
get into trouble,</i>

25
00:03:35,798 --> 00:03:38,050
<i>and why would you let her go
to that place alone?</i>

26
00:03:38,051 --> 00:03:41,261
<i>She said she was going home
because she wanted to rest.</i>

27
00:03:41,262 --> 00:03:43,305
<i>But you should have known
she was lying.</i>

28
00:03:43,306 --> 00:03:44,932
<i>She told you what you wanted to hear,</i>

29
00:03:44,933 --> 00:03:47,644
<i>and you didn't think
to check if it was true.</i>

30
00:03:48,186 --> 00:03:49,519
<i>I was an idiot.</i>

31
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:52,773
<i>We both were, and one of us
is out of a job because of it.</i>

32
00:03:52,774 --> 00:03:55,567
<i>You hated that job anyway,
so no big loss.</i>

33
00:03:55,568 --> 00:03:57,153
<i>But now she won't talk to us.</i>

34
00:04:28,226 --> 00:04:31,479
No, Hui-su! No! No!

35
00:04:32,105 --> 00:04:33,481
You're not gonna die.

36
00:04:50,790 --> 00:04:53,083
<i>When I finally
did come to my senses,</i>

37
00:04:53,084 --> 00:04:55,044
<i>time had already flown by.</i>

38
00:04:55,545 --> 00:04:59,090
<i>Everyone else seemed to be
living their lives to the fullest,</i>

39
00:04:59,674 --> 00:05:02,468
<i>while I seemed to be stuck in place.</i>

40
00:05:03,052 --> 00:05:05,637
<i>That's when I realized
that nothing changes</i>

41
00:05:05,638 --> 00:05:07,015
<i>if you don't do anything.</i>

42
00:05:08,516 --> 00:05:11,560
{\an8}<i>One day, I noticed
that the waterway of my life</i>

43
00:05:11,561 --> 00:05:13,354
{\an8}<i>had already changed.</i>

44
00:05:14,188 --> 00:05:17,149
{\an8}<i>Of course, our paths may become rough,</i>

45
00:05:17,150 --> 00:05:19,444
{\an8}<i>or we may run into obstacles,</i>

46
00:05:19,944 --> 00:05:23,031
<i>and there may be twists and turns
on the way,</i>

47
00:05:23,656 --> 00:05:27,159
<i>but if I keep flowing on my own way,
I'm sure I'll end up somewhere.</i>

48
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:30,079
<i>Whoever I find myself
to be at the end of that path...</i>

49
00:05:50,099 --> 00:05:52,727
I always swore
I wouldn't take on Mom's habits.

50
00:06:50,535 --> 00:06:52,203
He isn't there today?

51
00:06:58,376 --> 00:07:00,378
He didn't go to the office today?

52
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:02,796
<i>You weren't aware either, ma'am?</i>

53
00:07:04,215 --> 00:07:07,760
<i>Please contact us as soon as
you get in touch with Mr. Noh.</i>

54
00:07:08,803 --> 00:07:10,304
Yes, of course.

55
00:07:11,764 --> 00:07:12,932
JIN-PYO'S OFFICE

56
00:07:16,018 --> 00:07:17,812
Has my brother checked in with you?

57
00:07:20,022 --> 00:07:22,191
What about his work? Did they call you?

58
00:07:26,571 --> 00:07:27,572
Why?

59
00:07:28,197 --> 00:07:29,198
What is it?

60
00:07:30,575 --> 00:07:32,702
I noticed his passport is missing.

61
00:07:34,078 --> 00:07:35,788
What would he need it for?

62
00:07:36,372 --> 00:07:38,749
I'm not sure,
but his suitcase is gone too.

63
00:07:39,250 --> 00:07:42,043
You think he took a trip
without telling any of us?

64
00:07:42,044 --> 00:07:44,588
Uh, can't really say.

65
00:07:47,258 --> 00:07:49,469
Did you mention these things to his work?

66
00:07:51,262 --> 00:07:53,138
I did when they called a bit earlier.

67
00:07:53,139 --> 00:07:56,934
I'll call in some favors.
If you hear from him, let me know.

68
00:07:58,060 --> 00:07:59,061
Okay.

69
00:08:15,828 --> 00:08:17,413
Hey, you busy?

70
00:08:18,539 --> 00:08:22,043
Yeah, I need you to check
a departure record for me, if you could.

71
00:08:22,627 --> 00:08:24,252
Once they check his departure,

72
00:08:24,253 --> 00:08:27,465
Jin-pyo's office and your sister-in-law
will have to let it go.

73
00:08:28,007 --> 00:08:29,091
It'll work.

74
00:08:30,426 --> 00:08:31,427
Mm.

75
00:08:32,887 --> 00:08:33,930
Mm-hmm.

76
00:08:45,983 --> 00:08:50,404
INCIDENTS AND ACCIDENTS TOP STORIES

77
00:09:03,501 --> 00:09:07,505
UNIDENTIFIED MALE CORPSE, 30S

78
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:31,361
He deposited five billion won
a few days before leaving the country,

79
00:09:31,362 --> 00:09:33,406
and then withdrew a portion of it
from his bank.

80
00:09:34,448 --> 00:09:37,242
And it was in his personal account?

81
00:09:37,243 --> 00:09:38,326
- Really?
- Yes, sir.

82
00:09:38,327 --> 00:09:40,663
Anything you can tell us
would be very helpful.

83
00:09:42,540 --> 00:09:43,541
Well,

84
00:09:44,917 --> 00:09:48,587
I would say lately,
Mr. Noh was rather obsessed

85
00:09:48,588 --> 00:09:50,589
with bringing a new client on board.

86
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:51,840
<i>A wealthy artist.</i>

87
00:09:51,841 --> 00:09:53,300
<i>It was shaky at first,</i>

88
00:09:53,301 --> 00:09:56,053
<i>but he did manage to land the account
just before he left.</i>

89
00:09:56,887 --> 00:09:58,556
It's worth five billion.

90
00:10:00,182 --> 00:10:03,685
I can see now that he probably
had this in mind all along.

91
00:10:03,686 --> 00:10:07,565
Using his client's funds to fill
his own account and flee the country.

92
00:10:10,401 --> 00:10:11,318
Oh my.

93
00:10:11,319 --> 00:10:14,487
Are you saying
that your deputy branch manager

94
00:10:14,488 --> 00:10:18,117
lured that client
with the intention of stealing her money?

95
00:10:24,707 --> 00:10:28,002
So you just stood there
and let him walk out the door?

96
00:10:29,712 --> 00:10:32,255
Maybe if I'd been awake when he left,
I would have said something,

97
00:10:32,256 --> 00:10:34,633
but I took some pills to sleep
and didn't hear the alarm.

98
00:10:34,634 --> 00:10:36,594
Why are you using drugs?

99
00:10:39,347 --> 00:10:40,847
Even if you slept through it,

100
00:10:40,848 --> 00:10:44,310
why didn't you call anyone
the second you realized he was gone?

101
00:10:45,728 --> 00:10:48,813
Sometimes, Jin-pyo would go
on a weekend with friends

102
00:10:48,814 --> 00:10:50,982
without telling me,
then go straight to work.

103
00:10:50,983 --> 00:10:53,778
- I assumed it was something like that.
- You made yourself eggs?

104
00:10:55,780 --> 00:10:58,866
And here I am so worried
that I can't eat a thing.

105
00:11:03,287 --> 00:11:04,163
Honey.

106
00:11:06,457 --> 00:11:09,084
My son,
what's weighing on you so heavily?

107
00:11:09,085 --> 00:11:10,836
Who did this to you?

108
00:11:11,462 --> 00:11:12,755
Oh.

109
00:11:30,690 --> 00:11:31,774
Aren't you

110
00:11:32,775 --> 00:11:34,735
even worried he's all right?

111
00:11:36,862 --> 00:11:39,489
Getting footage
from Shanghai Airport wasn't easy.

112
00:11:39,490 --> 00:11:42,033
But hey, serve your friends,
serve your country, right?

113
00:11:44,829 --> 00:11:46,080
No way.

114
00:11:49,542 --> 00:11:50,793
A kid?

115
00:11:58,551 --> 00:11:59,677
Oh shit.

116
00:12:01,804 --> 00:12:03,597
Another mistress?

117
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:07,934
What the hell is going on?

118
00:12:11,397 --> 00:12:14,024
MOM

119
00:12:17,153 --> 00:12:17,986
Hi, Mom.

120
00:12:19,321 --> 00:12:20,573
Hui-su

121
00:12:21,949 --> 00:12:23,242
is unbelievable.

122
00:12:23,951 --> 00:12:25,994
<i>- She's acting strange.</i>

123
00:12:25,995 --> 00:12:28,204
While I was crying a river
in front of her,

124
00:12:28,205 --> 00:12:30,290
not one single tear fell down her cheek.

125
00:12:30,291 --> 00:12:33,794
You can't just show up at her house.
She's in shock.

126
00:12:35,004 --> 00:12:37,089
- <i>And Jin-pyo--</i>
- Did he call?

127
00:12:38,758 --> 00:12:39,966
<i>What about your brother?</i>

128
00:12:39,967 --> 00:12:41,051
Huh?

129
00:12:43,053 --> 00:12:46,181
Jin-pyo walked out on his own,
so leave Hui-su alone.

130
00:12:46,182 --> 00:12:48,224
He'll come crawling back eventually!

131
00:12:48,225 --> 00:12:50,728
Wait, Jin...

132
00:12:57,193 --> 00:12:58,652
Embezzlement?

133
00:12:59,403 --> 00:13:02,615
We showed Mrs. Jo
the results of our audit yesterday.

134
00:13:09,872 --> 00:13:14,125
Uh, I'm just surprised
that you could do an audit so quickly.

135
00:13:14,126 --> 00:13:17,086
Since integrity and trust
are paramount to our business,

136
00:13:17,087 --> 00:13:20,924
we've installed a system
that allows us to quickly investigate

137
00:13:20,925 --> 00:13:23,092
any instances of suspected misconduct,

138
00:13:23,093 --> 00:13:26,847
such as potential use of company funds
for personal use.

139
00:13:32,311 --> 00:13:34,813
AUDIT REPORT
NOH JIN-PYO EMBEZZLEMENT CASE

140
00:13:41,904 --> 00:13:43,738
DATES OF ENTRY AND EXIT

141
00:13:43,739 --> 00:13:47,116
In spite of Mr. Noh's embezzling
client funds and fleeing the country,

142
00:13:47,117 --> 00:13:49,619
we've decided
not to file criminal charges.

143
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:50,912
In the interest of all parties,

144
00:13:50,913 --> 00:13:53,916
we would prefer to handle the situation
and his dismissal quietly.

145
00:13:54,708 --> 00:13:57,126
We would also like to assure you
that we've taken this decision

146
00:13:57,127 --> 00:14:00,381
after thorough deliberation
and difficult discussions.

147
00:14:01,048 --> 00:14:06,178
Is it possible to wait just a bit longer
so he can explain when he gets back?

148
00:14:18,774 --> 00:14:19,608
Excuse me.

149
00:14:22,236 --> 00:14:23,987
They're waiting for you upstairs, Mrs. Jo.

150
00:14:23,988 --> 00:14:26,574
Okay. Thank you for letting me know.

151
00:14:27,908 --> 00:14:29,660
I'm told you're a detective?

152
00:14:30,619 --> 00:14:32,830
You are Mr. Noh's sister?

153
00:14:33,330 --> 00:14:35,499
An Myeong-ho. I work in his department.

154
00:14:38,127 --> 00:14:42,256
I apologize if I'm out of line,
but this situation doesn't make sense.

155
00:14:42,756 --> 00:14:44,465
I think it's worth looking into.

156
00:14:44,466 --> 00:14:46,217
Since you're a detective,
you could find out

157
00:14:46,218 --> 00:14:47,928
if he really did what they say.

158
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:51,639
I'll look into it. Thanks for telling us.

159
00:14:51,640 --> 00:14:53,308
Please call me if you have questions.

160
00:14:53,309 --> 00:14:54,518
Yeah.

161
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:12,786
ALPHA INVESTMENT & SECURITIES CO, LTD.
AN MYEONG-HO

162
00:15:25,341 --> 00:15:27,885
Uh, I'm not sure
I should listen to those guys.

163
00:15:29,470 --> 00:15:31,472
If you don't, he gets a record.

164
00:15:31,972 --> 00:15:34,892
I have no idea
what he was thinking, the idiot.

165
00:15:35,434 --> 00:15:37,018
You got lucky they wanna keep this quiet,

166
00:15:37,019 --> 00:15:39,187
so you don't wanna do anything
to piss them off.

167
00:15:39,188 --> 00:15:41,398
If they press charges, he's done for.

168
00:15:41,982 --> 00:15:44,400
I can't stand how they pretend
that this is hard for them

169
00:15:44,401 --> 00:15:46,736
when all they care about
is their reputation.

170
00:15:46,737 --> 00:15:48,739
It's a blessing in disguise though.

171
00:15:49,698 --> 00:15:53,410
'Cause if the police get involved...
it's over.

172
00:15:55,454 --> 00:15:56,288
Right.

173
00:15:57,206 --> 00:16:00,876
You need to lay low
and not do anything to attract suspicion.

174
00:16:01,418 --> 00:16:03,629
Stick to your routine and stay quiet.

175
00:16:04,672 --> 00:16:05,672
Suspicion?

176
00:16:05,673 --> 00:16:08,800
Your husband took off
after committing embezzlement,

177
00:16:08,801 --> 00:16:11,011
but if you filed for divorce
all of a sudden,

178
00:16:11,720 --> 00:16:15,390
you'd only be drawing more attention,
and they'll think you helped him do it.

179
00:16:15,391 --> 00:16:16,599
You know I didn't.

180
00:16:16,600 --> 00:16:18,185
Yeah, but they don't.

181
00:16:21,605 --> 00:16:24,608
Hui-su, Jin-pyo will be back.

182
00:16:25,901 --> 00:16:26,860
Yeah.

183
00:16:29,571 --> 00:16:30,739
You good to get home?

184
00:16:32,950 --> 00:16:34,868
I'll be fine. Thank you.

185
00:16:52,302 --> 00:16:53,387
Yes. Hello?

186
00:16:53,887 --> 00:16:58,350
About the family background check?
I'll send the consent form today.

187
00:17:04,106 --> 00:17:06,608
- <i>Hey, how's it going?</i>
- I think it's working.

188
00:17:08,277 --> 00:17:09,528
You did so well, Hui-su.

189
00:17:10,612 --> 00:17:12,948
I can't believe it's actually going
like we planned.

190
00:17:14,033 --> 00:17:15,743
You can relax now. It's done.

191
00:17:17,244 --> 00:17:18,245
Mm-hmm.

192
00:17:34,887 --> 00:17:37,890
MOM

193
00:18:05,167 --> 00:18:08,087
Wow, it looks so good on you.

194
00:18:12,424 --> 00:18:14,092
I'm not sure.

195
00:18:14,093 --> 00:18:16,636
It's been so long
since I wore anything like this.

196
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:21,809
You look very pretty, ma'am.

197
00:18:34,404 --> 00:18:36,489
I almost didn't recognize you.

198
00:18:36,490 --> 00:18:38,075
It's the new Hui-su.

199
00:18:39,201 --> 00:18:41,285
I said let's splurge, and you chose here?

200
00:18:41,286 --> 00:18:43,746
I miss the days
when we came here all the time.

201
00:18:43,747 --> 00:18:47,041
And when their <i>tteokbokki</i> calls your name,
you have to answer.

202
00:18:47,042 --> 00:18:49,085
Yep, absolutely. Come on.

203
00:18:49,086 --> 00:18:51,003
- I'm buying you all you can eat.
- Really?

204
00:18:51,004 --> 00:18:52,256
Really.

205
00:18:52,840 --> 00:18:54,465
I'm taking you up on that offer.

206
00:18:54,466 --> 00:18:56,760
You better.
I feel like stuffing my face too.

207
00:19:46,226 --> 00:19:47,227
Hui-su.

208
00:19:48,645 --> 00:19:50,731
You wanna try a little sip?

209
00:19:51,732 --> 00:19:52,566
Mm-mm.

210
00:19:54,234 --> 00:19:55,401
Mm...

211
00:19:58,197 --> 00:19:59,531
Come on!

212
00:20:02,910 --> 00:20:04,328
Where did it go?

213
00:21:51,226 --> 00:21:55,230
In future pictures of Mom,
I want to see her smile.

214
00:21:57,941 --> 00:21:58,942
What?

215
00:22:00,444 --> 00:22:03,529
You interrupt my exercise
to talk about pictures?

216
00:22:03,530 --> 00:22:07,491
It's not enough you give me grief about
your mother, I need to make her smile?

217
00:22:07,492 --> 00:22:09,452
I went through every picture,

218
00:22:09,453 --> 00:22:11,829
from kindergarten to college graduation,

219
00:22:11,830 --> 00:22:14,458
and Mom isn't smiling
in a single one of them.

220
00:22:14,958 --> 00:22:17,836
That says everything
about how badly you've treated her.

221
00:22:19,296 --> 00:22:22,631
I'm not gonna stand here
and listen to your silly stories.

222
00:22:22,632 --> 00:22:23,716
Go back home to bed.

223
00:22:23,717 --> 00:22:26,219
I won't let you dismiss this as nothing!

224
00:22:27,888 --> 00:22:29,597
My childhood was not nothing.

225
00:22:29,598 --> 00:22:32,934
What you made us live through
affects us to this day.

226
00:22:33,477 --> 00:22:36,479
You terrified us.
Mom and I lived in the hell you created--

227
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:40,650
You're the one creating hell for me now
with this nonsense about your childhood.

228
00:22:42,110 --> 00:22:44,987
When I'm six feet under,
don't start crying for me then.

229
00:22:44,988 --> 00:22:46,531
Don't you worry.

230
00:22:52,162 --> 00:22:53,622
When you're dead and buried,

231
00:22:54,498 --> 00:22:56,249
all we'll feel is relief.

232
00:23:02,923 --> 00:23:07,177
If you <i>ever</i> put a hand on Mom again,
I will no longer speak to you.

233
00:23:07,677 --> 00:23:09,095
And my brother won't either.

234
00:23:09,096 --> 00:23:11,847
We will not let our mother
keep living with a monster.

235
00:23:11,848 --> 00:23:13,392
We'll turn our backs on you for good.

236
00:24:14,286 --> 00:24:15,704
It's safe to come out.

237
00:24:34,347 --> 00:24:35,474
Eun-su.

238
00:24:38,602 --> 00:24:40,186
It's so early. What's wrong?

239
00:24:40,187 --> 00:24:41,605
I'm fine.

240
00:24:42,314 --> 00:24:45,150
I didn't know you were coming.
What's going on?

241
00:24:47,027 --> 00:24:48,737
Can we get rid of this thing?

242
00:24:54,409 --> 00:24:55,327
Huh?

243
00:24:57,370 --> 00:24:59,164
I'm sick of seeing it here.

244
00:25:12,344 --> 00:25:14,638
Okay. Let's toss it.

245
00:25:16,348 --> 00:25:18,390
We'll carry it out right now.

246
00:25:32,781 --> 00:25:33,823
Well done,

247
00:25:35,242 --> 00:25:36,326
Eun-su.

248
00:26:47,522 --> 00:26:49,232
<i>The doors are opening.</i>

249
00:26:58,533 --> 00:27:00,201
You're looking pretty cute today.

250
00:27:00,702 --> 00:27:01,703
Huh?

251
00:27:04,873 --> 00:27:05,957
You too.

252
00:27:07,542 --> 00:27:08,585
I know.

253
00:27:15,508 --> 00:27:19,303
SANGAE NURSING HOME

254
00:27:20,388 --> 00:27:23,766
These days, I drink my coffee
in the cup you bought me,

255
00:27:23,767 --> 00:27:25,268
the one with flowers.

256
00:27:26,061 --> 00:27:29,397
It tastes so good, full of memories.

257
00:27:30,732 --> 00:27:33,360
When I had constant mouth sores,
everything tasted bitter.

258
00:27:34,319 --> 00:27:35,528
Even water.

259
00:27:36,529 --> 00:27:38,281
But now it tastes sweet.

260
00:27:52,087 --> 00:27:54,631
Don't worry. It's all healed up.

261
00:27:58,259 --> 00:27:59,551
Hmm? You like it?

262
00:27:59,552 --> 00:28:00,804
It's nice.

263
00:28:02,806 --> 00:28:05,934
Let me just finish up,
and I'll take a picture.

264
00:28:09,646 --> 00:28:11,398
I thought I could trust him.

265
00:28:11,898 --> 00:28:13,358
I feel like it's my fault.

266
00:28:15,610 --> 00:28:17,320
They reimbursed it all.

267
00:28:21,366 --> 00:28:24,619
It's better for them to pay
than losing me as a client.

268
00:28:25,704 --> 00:28:28,081
I was never worried
about that money, anyway.

269
00:28:29,124 --> 00:28:30,958
My only concern was word getting out

270
00:28:30,959 --> 00:28:33,753
and my husband finding out
about my sizable slush fund.

271
00:28:34,254 --> 00:28:36,047
It's a good solution for me.

272
00:28:39,926 --> 00:28:41,594
I'm glad it worked out for her.

273
00:28:42,595 --> 00:28:44,848
I would've felt bad
if she had lost everything.

274
00:28:45,515 --> 00:28:47,434
It is good that it all worked out, but

275
00:28:48,351 --> 00:28:50,937
I do feel guilty about taking advantage.

276
00:28:51,521 --> 00:28:52,480
Mm-hmm.

277
00:28:56,568 --> 00:28:58,153
The soup is great, isn't it?

278
00:29:04,033 --> 00:29:05,743
Why do you keep doing that?

279
00:29:05,744 --> 00:29:07,786
Uh, I don't know.

280
00:29:07,787 --> 00:29:09,622
- Ah! I'm such a klutz.
- Oh!

281
00:29:20,175 --> 00:29:23,178
I still feel like
I'll hear him coming in the door.

282
00:29:27,599 --> 00:29:28,808
You mean Jin-pyo?

283
00:29:30,602 --> 00:29:31,519
Mm-hmm.

284
00:29:35,648 --> 00:29:38,777
How would you like
to start illustrating again?

285
00:29:42,405 --> 00:29:43,781
I've thought about it, actually.

286
00:29:43,782 --> 00:29:45,616
Mm-hmm.
You should give your publisher a call.

287
00:29:45,617 --> 00:29:46,576
I need

288
00:29:48,077 --> 00:29:49,579
to start somewhere new.

289
00:29:50,079 --> 00:29:51,831
Where no one knows who I am.

290
00:29:52,332 --> 00:29:54,250
And maybe start a new life for myself.

291
00:30:04,594 --> 00:30:06,054
It's at the end, down there.

292
00:30:12,977 --> 00:30:14,561
It's crazy here, so be careful.

293
00:30:14,562 --> 00:30:15,647
Okay.

294
00:30:23,363 --> 00:30:24,447
Boxes.

295
00:30:47,554 --> 00:30:53,309
JINGANG CHINESE MARKET

296
00:30:59,732 --> 00:31:02,443
MISSED CALLS
MR. JIN SO-BAEK

297
00:31:04,195 --> 00:31:05,947
I wonder what he wanted.

298
00:31:12,328 --> 00:31:16,999
{\an8}RECRUITING WAREHOUSE STAFF
BEGINNERS WELCOME

299
00:31:25,967 --> 00:31:27,509
Hey, it's been a while.

300
00:31:27,510 --> 00:31:30,053
- Yes.
- Need to finish this up.

301
00:31:30,054 --> 00:31:31,763
Are you checking the order list?

302
00:31:31,764 --> 00:31:34,225
- Looks like they actually got it right.
- Ah.

303
00:31:36,019 --> 00:31:37,978
Hey, move that a bit more to the side.

304
00:31:37,979 --> 00:31:41,064
- Not yet, but I'm watching for it.
- Here, here, here.

305
00:31:41,065 --> 00:31:44,319
<i>Grab another cup of coffee.
I'll text you when we're ready.</i>

306
00:31:45,361 --> 00:31:48,488
I can't do this on my own.
Somebody listen to me. I need help.

307
00:31:48,489 --> 00:31:50,074
Make sure the aisle is clear.

308
00:31:57,498 --> 00:32:00,668
Best way to clear your head
is to get your body moving.

309
00:32:04,339 --> 00:32:05,548
You're looking for help?

310
00:32:15,183 --> 00:32:19,187
CURRICULUM VITAE
JO HUI-SU

311
00:32:47,507 --> 00:32:50,510
The work we do here
involves a fair amount of physical labor.

312
00:32:52,887 --> 00:32:55,389
You won't be sitting around,
writing fairy tales, you know?

313
00:32:55,390 --> 00:32:58,559
She's not as fragile as she looks,
and her hands can do magic.

314
00:33:00,770 --> 00:33:03,230
I moved a few of
your boxes around while I was waiting.

315
00:33:03,231 --> 00:33:04,899
I know I can do it.

316
00:33:05,942 --> 00:33:08,528
I like to move my furniture around.
I'm strong.

317
00:33:09,862 --> 00:33:11,905
What kind of work do you have for her?

318
00:33:11,906 --> 00:33:14,367
I need to replace Jang Kang,
since he quit.

319
00:33:18,746 --> 00:33:20,748
I think you met him in the warehouse.

320
00:33:25,545 --> 00:33:26,796
Oh, yeah.

321
00:33:28,548 --> 00:33:30,008
He took off back home.

322
00:33:33,845 --> 00:33:35,096
That's great.

323
00:33:44,230 --> 00:33:46,399
Let's see.

324
00:33:48,026 --> 00:33:51,987
I think I just happen to have an opening
for someone to prepare deliveries

325
00:33:51,988 --> 00:33:53,989
and make sure the shelves are stocked.

326
00:34:01,414 --> 00:34:04,207
You would be working in the warehouse
on your feet most of the day,

327
00:34:04,208 --> 00:34:05,543
not at a desk.

328
00:34:07,837 --> 00:34:09,379
I prefer to be active.

329
00:34:09,380 --> 00:34:11,883
Does your husband know
you're applying here?

330
00:34:13,801 --> 00:34:15,178
You do have a husband?

331
00:34:18,765 --> 00:34:20,807
- Uh, her--
- No, we're separated.

332
00:34:27,815 --> 00:34:29,317
Sometimes there's overtime.

333
00:34:30,902 --> 00:34:32,570
My schedule is quite flexible.

334
00:34:47,085 --> 00:34:50,254
You'll be on probation for a month.
Give the bookkeeper your information.

335
00:34:52,548 --> 00:34:53,840
This is great. Thank you.

336
00:34:53,841 --> 00:34:55,176
Thank you, Mr. Jin.

337
00:35:04,811 --> 00:35:06,186
UNIT 1501
CALL

338
00:35:49,480 --> 00:35:51,439
For you to wear
on your first day of work.

339
00:35:51,440 --> 00:35:54,777
The color will give you
a little pop of energy, like it used to.

340
00:35:56,821 --> 00:35:58,531
You're the best.

341
00:36:18,843 --> 00:36:20,386
Going somewhere, ma'am?

342
00:36:20,887 --> 00:36:21,804
Oh, yes.

343
00:36:23,431 --> 00:36:24,640
Have a great day.

344
00:36:38,696 --> 00:36:41,032
November 10th, morning.

345
00:36:41,616 --> 00:36:45,036
Tan jacket, and jeans, lipstick,

346
00:36:45,870 --> 00:36:47,079
ponytail,

347
00:36:47,997 --> 00:36:49,332
brown purse.

348
00:36:49,874 --> 00:36:53,043
We plan to expand the Key Program
in the first quarter of next year,

349
00:36:53,044 --> 00:36:55,086
to have more workshops
for our prestige clients...

350
00:36:59,634 --> 00:37:00,926
Sorry about that.

351
00:37:00,927 --> 00:37:02,802
...that involve luxury brand experts.

352
00:37:06,807 --> 00:37:09,518
Answer. It could be an important client.

353
00:37:10,519 --> 00:37:12,313
Right. Thank you so much.

354
00:37:13,147 --> 00:37:14,314
Yes. Hello?

355
00:37:14,315 --> 00:37:16,858
<i>Is this Ms. Jo, saleswoman at Lavie?</i>

356
00:37:16,859 --> 00:37:18,068
Yes, this is.

357
00:37:18,069 --> 00:37:20,570
<i>This is Detective Yu from the police.</i>

358
00:37:20,571 --> 00:37:22,405
<i>Do you have a minute to talk?</i>

359
00:37:22,406 --> 00:37:23,532
It's the police?

360
00:37:27,578 --> 00:37:29,538
Uh, so sorry.

361
00:37:34,043 --> 00:37:36,544
I wouldn't wanna anger him.
He has deep pockets.

362
00:37:36,545 --> 00:37:39,673
He went after the journalist
who wrote that Mrs. Kang killed herself

363
00:37:39,674 --> 00:37:40,882
due to his abuse.

364
00:37:42,677 --> 00:37:46,096
It was him.
She couldn't take another beating, sir.

365
00:37:46,097 --> 00:37:49,558
Listen, if you go to the police station,
he's gonna know.

366
00:37:54,438 --> 00:37:56,064
They're probably asking you to come in

367
00:37:56,065 --> 00:37:58,525
'cause you're the last person
who talked to her that day

368
00:37:58,526 --> 00:38:01,153
aside from her family, the day she died.

369
00:38:02,029 --> 00:38:03,863
Think carefully, Ms. Jo.

370
00:38:03,864 --> 00:38:06,157
Do you know how much
Mr. Kwon spends in here?

371
00:38:06,158 --> 00:38:08,159
I'm sure I don't need to spell it out.

372
00:38:08,160 --> 00:38:10,328
You're the member of the VIP sales team

373
00:38:10,329 --> 00:38:12,914
who understands his impact
nearly as well as I do.

374
00:38:12,915 --> 00:38:14,958
Do you know what our numbers
would be without him?

375
00:38:14,959 --> 00:38:18,378
- Numbers aren't what's important--
- You didn't help when she asked you!

376
00:38:18,379 --> 00:38:21,465
You had no trouble staying quiet.
She's dead. That's it.

377
00:38:29,807 --> 00:38:31,559
This is what you're going to say.

378
00:38:32,643 --> 00:38:35,062
"I didn't see any evidence of abuse.”

379
00:38:36,022 --> 00:38:37,106
"None at all."

380
00:38:50,536 --> 00:38:51,787
Good evening, miss.

381
00:38:56,208 --> 00:38:57,292
Good evening, sir.

382
00:38:57,293 --> 00:39:00,128
A token of Mr. Kwon's appreciation
for your help.

383
00:39:03,507 --> 00:39:05,676
I haven't done anything
to earn his thanks.

384
00:39:07,678 --> 00:39:09,304
Please take it back. I can't accept.

385
00:39:09,305 --> 00:39:10,723
He will insist.

386
00:39:21,692 --> 00:39:22,777
Hold on!

387
00:39:42,213 --> 00:39:43,756
What are you still doing here?

388
00:39:44,382 --> 00:39:47,593
Oh. I hope I'm not bothering you.
I thought you were gone.

389
00:39:49,261 --> 00:39:50,804
I forgot my wallet.

390
00:39:50,805 --> 00:39:51,889
Ah.

391
00:40:19,959 --> 00:40:21,544
You've done enough. Go home.

392
00:40:22,044 --> 00:40:24,295
If you don't mind,
I'd like to finish this.

393
00:40:24,296 --> 00:40:26,507
Unless you don't want me to stay.

394
00:40:28,676 --> 00:40:30,845
I don't have any manager
or executive positions.

395
00:40:32,054 --> 00:40:32,929
Sir?

396
00:40:32,930 --> 00:40:35,099
Eun-su wants to be an executive.

397
00:40:35,599 --> 00:40:38,018
If that's your goal here,
you'll be disappointed.

398
00:40:38,811 --> 00:40:40,187
What's wrong with this?

399
00:40:40,855 --> 00:40:43,357
That's not why I'm here at all.

400
00:40:50,948 --> 00:40:52,867
Oh, you're working late too?

401
00:40:53,534 --> 00:40:55,911
We're going out for dinner.
Would you like to join us?

402
00:40:57,204 --> 00:40:58,080
I could eat.

403
00:41:00,458 --> 00:41:01,792
Ready?

404
00:41:03,127 --> 00:41:05,337
Oh, just let me grab my stuff.

405
00:41:10,593 --> 00:41:13,512
One of my favorite clients
told me the food here is amazing.

406
00:41:17,391 --> 00:41:19,894
I'm sure it's true. Please dig in.

407
00:41:25,608 --> 00:41:28,110
Eun-su, it's not cooked yet.

408
00:41:30,029 --> 00:41:33,699
Ah, I guess I'm too hungry.
I skipped lunch today.

409
00:41:38,454 --> 00:41:39,955
Uh, excuse me?

410
00:41:40,498 --> 00:41:41,874
Could you bring us...

411
00:41:44,752 --> 00:41:47,129
I think we should
give it time. We'll hear back.

412
00:42:08,776 --> 00:42:10,486
I need to use the ladies' room.

413
00:42:16,033 --> 00:42:17,409
Don't be afraid.

414
00:42:21,038 --> 00:42:21,955
Mr. Kwon.

415
00:42:24,166 --> 00:42:25,875
This is the ladies' room, sir.

416
00:42:25,876 --> 00:42:28,045
I know. My assistant's watching the door.

417
00:42:35,177 --> 00:42:37,262
If this is about your wife,
I can't talk to you.

418
00:42:39,014 --> 00:42:41,308
We need to protect my wife's honor.

419
00:42:42,560 --> 00:42:45,812
Suicide caused by domestic violence.

420
00:42:45,813 --> 00:42:47,022
Huh.

421
00:42:48,315 --> 00:42:49,525
Ms. Jo,

422
00:42:50,401 --> 00:42:52,778
you knew her shoe size, nothing else.

423
00:42:54,280 --> 00:42:55,990
I regret not helping her

424
00:42:57,241 --> 00:42:58,534
when I could have.

425
00:42:59,159 --> 00:43:00,786
I'll never forgive myself for that.

426
00:43:04,164 --> 00:43:05,457
So,

427
00:43:07,376 --> 00:43:10,671
you're gonna do something
more regrettable?

428
00:43:13,299 --> 00:43:14,883
I sent you a "thank you."

429
00:43:16,635 --> 00:43:20,264
I intend to testify
and tell the police everything I saw.

430
00:43:31,692 --> 00:43:33,319
They'll hear about this too.

431
00:43:51,754 --> 00:43:54,632
- Shit.
- You can't go in there! Hey! Hey!

432
00:43:55,633 --> 00:43:57,009
Mr. Jin!

433
00:44:07,436 --> 00:44:09,355
It seems like I caught you in the act.

434
00:44:10,230 --> 00:44:11,148
Look...

435
00:44:12,066 --> 00:44:14,776
Please don't, sir!

436
00:44:14,777 --> 00:44:18,113
You wanna take a swing at me,
or say you're good and walk away?

437
00:44:19,907 --> 00:44:23,243
Yeah, I'm good.

438
00:44:24,787 --> 00:44:25,953
Eun-su!

439
00:44:25,954 --> 00:44:28,540
It's all right. I'm okay now.

440
00:44:30,709 --> 00:44:32,211
- Really.
- Are you sure?

441
00:44:38,759 --> 00:44:39,718
Hold on.

442
00:44:40,219 --> 00:44:42,637
He's the reason
I didn't get my hangover soup

443
00:44:42,638 --> 00:44:44,597
or the barbecue that looked so good.

444
00:44:44,598 --> 00:44:46,141
What a big asshole.

445
00:44:50,020 --> 00:44:51,646
You showed up at the right time, sir.

446
00:44:51,647 --> 00:44:54,608
I could use someone like you
to help me run things.

447
00:45:07,955 --> 00:45:09,580
What's your plan? Huh?

448
00:45:09,581 --> 00:45:11,583
What do you wanna do? Talk to me.

449
00:45:15,212 --> 00:45:16,672
I wanna put an end to this.

450
00:45:17,256 --> 00:45:18,756
You're going to the police?

451
00:45:18,757 --> 00:45:21,510
He could come after you again.
It's too dangerous.

452
00:45:29,059 --> 00:45:30,728
She's made up her mind.

453
00:45:31,395 --> 00:45:34,732
I guess you might as well
try to ease your conscience.

454
00:45:36,442 --> 00:45:37,693
Do... do you have to?

455
00:45:39,528 --> 00:45:41,155
It's the only way.

456
00:45:51,540 --> 00:45:54,042
Here you were
taking care of me when all along...

457
00:45:58,297 --> 00:45:59,923
you had your own worries.

458
00:46:03,844 --> 00:46:05,512
Oh, no. What...

459
00:46:12,352 --> 00:46:14,270
Where's all this coming from?

460
00:46:14,271 --> 00:46:16,564
Ugh, I feel so selfish.

461
00:46:16,565 --> 00:46:19,359
It's times like these
you need a little clattering.

462
00:46:26,867 --> 00:46:27,701
You'll love this.

463
00:46:33,499 --> 00:46:35,793
- Ooh.
- Wow.

464
00:46:40,005 --> 00:46:41,131
Wanna give it a shot?

465
00:46:42,341 --> 00:46:43,383
Oh...

466
00:47:17,125 --> 00:47:18,043
Oh!

467
00:47:19,837 --> 00:47:21,463
She does have magic hands.

468
00:47:23,215 --> 00:47:26,385
You know, the sound is relaxing somehow.

469
00:47:28,428 --> 00:47:31,014
Looks like my new hire
has some hidden talents.

470
00:47:45,654 --> 00:47:47,572
Why am I the only one
who can't do it?

471
00:47:47,573 --> 00:47:49,615
I'd like to go finish what I was doing.

472
00:47:49,616 --> 00:47:51,660
Such a hard worker.

473
00:47:57,833 --> 00:48:01,670
Jang Kang quitting out of the blue
really left us understaffed, you know?

474
00:48:03,005 --> 00:48:05,507
She won't quit out of the blue, will she?

475
00:48:08,051 --> 00:48:09,094
Course not.

476
00:48:09,761 --> 00:48:11,138
Are you thirsty?

477
00:48:15,934 --> 00:48:19,395
Your calendar seems to be stuck.
It's always the same date.

478
00:48:19,396 --> 00:48:20,731
Don't touch that!

479
00:48:24,568 --> 00:48:25,611
Okay.

480
00:48:31,992 --> 00:48:34,870
It's my son's birthday.

481
00:48:36,830 --> 00:48:38,624
And also the day he died.

482
00:48:42,377 --> 00:48:44,046
You two should go home.

483
00:48:46,423 --> 00:48:49,176
We'll finish up tomorrow.
Come on, so I can lock up.

484
00:49:08,028 --> 00:49:10,614
I know what it's like to lose a child.

485
00:49:29,341 --> 00:49:30,509
My condolences.

486
00:49:36,056 --> 00:49:37,140
And the same to you.

487
00:49:52,280 --> 00:49:53,657
Clatter, clatter.

488
00:49:56,910 --> 00:49:58,328
Clatter, clatter.

489
00:50:02,916 --> 00:50:04,459
Clatter, clatter.

490
00:50:30,402 --> 00:50:31,319
Let's go.

491
00:50:40,954 --> 00:50:45,041
INTERVIEW ROOM, VISITATION ROOM

492
00:50:45,042 --> 00:50:46,251
<i>Shall we begin?</i>

493
00:50:48,670 --> 00:50:49,546
Yeah.

494
00:50:56,595 --> 00:50:58,805
- I'll order. You grab us seats.
- Okay.

495
00:50:59,306 --> 00:51:02,224
<i>...the man driving the car
was identified as Kwon Seong-cheol,</i>

496
00:51:02,225 --> 00:51:04,602
<i>the victim's husband and wealthy CEO.</i>

497
00:51:04,603 --> 00:51:06,729
<i>Following the incident,
controversy emerged</i>

498
00:51:06,730 --> 00:51:10,775
<i>over whether the victim committed suicide
by running into the car's path, or...</i>

499
00:51:10,776 --> 00:51:11,818
What?

500
00:51:13,445 --> 00:51:16,280
- Someone else got the promotion.
- Huh?

501
00:51:16,281 --> 00:51:18,783
<i>The victim is believed
to have taken her own life</i>

502
00:51:18,784 --> 00:51:20,868
<i>due to prolonged domestic abuse.</i>

503
00:51:20,869 --> 00:51:22,411
Eun-su didn't get it?

504
00:51:22,412 --> 00:51:24,663
<i>We bring you
this special report.</i>

505
00:51:24,664 --> 00:51:28,292
<i>Initially, the incident
was considered a tragic traffic accident,</i>

506
00:51:28,293 --> 00:51:30,544
